From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:15:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Put a disabled EHCI controller in D3
 before hiding it

usb_ehci_disable(), which the SMM handler runs when it routes every port
to xHCI, sets DCh[0] (the clock gating step that usb_ehci_clock_gating()
leaves for a disabled controller), puts the controller in D3hot with PME
disabled and clears its BAR, then sets its function disable bit.
pch_disable_devfn() only sets the bit: an EHCI controller turned off in
the devicetree or by the mainboard code is hidden in D0, without that
clock gating step.

Take the same steps there for both EHCI controllers. pch_enable() has
already cleared their command register.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.c
index 80473332ef..76392d8419 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.c
@@ -84,6 +84,19 @@ static void pch_enable_d3hot(struct device *dev)
 	pci_or_config32(dev, PCH_PCS, PCH_PCS_PS_D3HOT);
 }
 
+/* As usb_ehci_disable() in SMM, before the function disable bit */
+static void pch_disable_ehci(struct device *dev)
+{
+	/* Dx:F0:DCh[0] = 1b when the EHCI controller is disabled */
+	pci_or_config32(dev, 0xdc, 1 << 0);
+
+	/* D3hot, PME disabled */
+	pci_update_config16(dev, EHCI_PWR_CTL_STS, ~(PWR_CTL_ENABLE_PME | PWR_CTL_SET_MASK),
+			    PWR_CTL_SET_D3);
+
+	pci_write_config32(dev, PCI_BASE_ADDRESS_0, 0);
+}
+
 /* Set bit in function disable register to hide this device */
 void pch_disable_devfn(struct device *dev)
 {
@@ -142,6 +155,7 @@ void pch_disable_devfn(struct device *dev)
 		RCBA32_OR(BUC, PCH_DISABLE_GBE);
 		break;
 	case PCI_DEVFN(26, 0): /* EHCI #2 */
+		pch_disable_ehci(dev);
 		RCBA32_OR(FD, PCH_DISABLE_EHCI2);
 		break;
 	case PCI_DEVFN(27, 0): /* HD Audio Controller */
@@ -158,6 +172,7 @@ void pch_disable_devfn(struct device *dev)
 		RCBA32_OR(FD, PCH_DISABLE_PCIE(PCI_FUNC(dev->path.pci.devfn)));
 		break;
 	case PCI_DEVFN(29, 0): /* EHCI #1 */
+		pch_disable_ehci(dev);
 		RCBA32_OR(FD, PCH_DISABLE_EHCI1);
 		break;
 	case PCI_DEVFN(31, 0): /* LPC */
-- 
